  "name": "Qualify, log and route inbound WhatsApp leads with OpenAI",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "st-header-01",
      "name": "Sticky Note 01",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -80,
        -496
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 1200,
        "height": 256,
        "content": "## Qualify, log & route inbound WhatsApp leads with AI\nEvery inbound WhatsApp message is classified as **buyer / job_seeker / spam**, logged to a sheet, and routed: buyers get an instant reply and you get a hot-lead alert.\n**Setup:**\n1. Point your WhatsApp provider's inbound webhook (POST) at the *WhatsApp Lead Intake* node.\n2. Add your OpenAI credential on the *OpenAI Chat Model* node.\n3. Pick your spreadsheet on the *Google Sheets* node — columns: Phone, Name, Message, Segment, Intent, Confidence, Reasoning, ReceivedAt, NeedsReview.\n4. Set your own number in *Notify Owner* (replace OWNER-PHONE) and connect a WAHA Header Auth credential on the three send nodes."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "st-receive-02",
      "name": "Sticky Note 02",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -80,
        -208
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 480,
        "height": 400,
        "content": "### 1. Receive & extract\nThe webhook accepts any WhatsApp provider payload (WAHA, Cloud API, Twilio…).\n*Extract Message* pulls out `message`, `phone`, `name` — adjust these three expressions to your provider's field names."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "st-classify-03",
      "name": "Sticky Note 03",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        496,
        -208
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 432,
        "height": 656,
        "content": "### 2. Classify with AI\nThe agent returns strict JSON: segment, intent_summary, confidence, reasoning.\nTune the *system message* to your business (e.g. add a `partner` segment), or swap the model for a cheaper one."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "st-log-04",
      "name": "Sticky Note 04",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        960,
        -208
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 6,
        "width": 480,
        "height": 416,
        "content": "### 3. Log to Google Sheets\n*Flatten Result* maps the AI output to flat columns.\nThe Sheets node **appends or updates** matching on Phone, so repeat messages update the same row instead of duplicating."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "st-reply-05",
      "name": "Sticky Note 05",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2208,
        -208
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 256,
        "height": 400,
        "content": "### 5. Done — respond\nEvery branch returns `{status, segment}` to the calling platform."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
